<%# The app-ladder row for /deployments: one card per three-rung repo, showing
    where each application sits on `accepted → release → main`.

    WHY IT EXISTS. An application's progress along the ladder is decoupled from the
    Next Release card. Work sits merged on `accepted` for hours before a sweep
    promotes it, and between releases Next Release reads "none active" while
    several repos quietly hold unshipped work. That in-between state had no
    surface at all — this is it.

    The row renders four cards today (the registry's three-rung repos) and grows on
    its own as satellites are registered; nothing here is hardcoded.

    Locals: cards - Array<Ci::AppLadder::Card>, already sorted worst-first. %>
<% cards = local_assigns.fetch(:cards, []) %>
<% if cards.any? %>
  <div class="mb-6" data-test="app-ladder-row">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-2">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Applications</h2>
      <span class="text-[10px] text-muted"><%= pluralize(cards.count, "repo") %> on the ladder</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid min-w-0 grid-cols-1 gap-4 items-stretch sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
      <% cards.each do |card| %>
        <%= render "app_ladder_card", card: card, card_class: "h-full min-w-0" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
